  "body": "Problem: A lot of APIs rely on \"[transient activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#activation-consuming-api)\" to work, and there are special failure cases that need to be checked by \"[consuming the user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#consume-user-activation)\" at particular moments in time. To get around this right now, WPT (for instance) is using hacks trying to `requestFullscreen()` and then cancelling the request (which is not standardized to actually consume the user activation, making the situation worse).  \r\n\r\nIt would be great if Web Driver provided a means to artificially \"consume user activation\", thus invalidating the transient activation. \r\n\r\nRelated discussion:\r\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/36481",
